    <h2>What Is the Confetti Cake Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Confetti Cake Blizzard is the birthday-cake-in-a-cup Blizzard — colorful cake pieces with rainbow sprinkles distributed throughout DQ soft serve. The cake pieces add a soft, vanilla-cake texture that pairs well with the creaminess of the soft serve. The sprinkles add color and a very slight texture crunch. It is the sweetest and most dessert-forward of the Summer 2026 seasonal lineup.</p>
  <p>See all Summer 2026 seasonal Blizzards on <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a> or the <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Best Occasion for the Confetti Cake Blizzard</h2>
  <p>The Confetti Cake Blizzard is a natural choice for birthday celebrations, especially if a <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-8inch">full DQ Cake</a> is too large for the group. For a solo birthday treat or a small group of two or three, ordering Confetti Cake Blizzards is a lower-cost alternative to a full ice cream cake.</p>
  <h2>Other Summer 2026 Seasonal Blizzards</h2>
  <p>The Summer 2026 seasonal rotation also includes the <a href="/items/dipped-strawberry-cheesecake-blizzard">Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake Blizzard</a>, the <a href="/items/smores-blizzard">S'mores Blizzard</a>, the <a href="/items/cotton-candy-blizzard">Cotton Candy Blizzard</a>, and the Mixing Bowl Mashup and Swicy Pineapple Tajín® Blizzards.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Confetti Cake Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>490</td><td>Sweet cake pieces + sprinkles</td></tr><tr><td>Cotton Candy Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>460</td><td>Lighter, sugar-spun sweetness</td></tr><tr><td>S'mores Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>500</td><td>Campfire flavors, more complex</td></tr><tr><td>Oreo® Cookie Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>420</td><td>Year-round, lower price</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (4.49) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (5.29) at 490 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

